cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Behavioral CCC: A Behavioral Structure Paradigm for Intelligent Systems"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe

repository-code: "https://github.com/sizhet/Behavioral-CCC"
abstract: >
  Behavioral CCC (Behavioral Common Concept Core) introduces a structural
  paradigm for modeling behavior and decision trajectories in intelligent
  systems. The framework extends structural intelligence concepts from
  static knowledge representation to behavioral structure modeling.
  It provides a unified interpretation of diverse AI systems, including
  large language model reasoning, AI coding assistants, agents, rule
  engines, and decision systems, by framing intelligence as the selection
  of behavioral trajectories under goals and constraints.

keywords:
  - structural intelligence
  - behavioral structure
  - decision trajectories
  - rule systems
  - AI agents
  - LLM reasoning
  - AI coding

